WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.509
If both paths return the same output, what exactly makes one eager and the other lazy?

q0002
00:00:08.509 --> 00:00:17.929
This episode has one job: Eager and lazy paths preserve exact semantics while placing aligned materialization work at different points in the construction timeline.

q0003
00:00:17.929 --> 00:00:27.349
We build on Explicit dense CM versus CM-IR, CM-IR nodes, sharing, and roots; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:35.858
Eager work happens during construction; lazy work is deferred until the requested result must be materialized.

q0005
00:00:35.858 --> 00:00:43.865
Watch for the label eager materialization; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:43.865 --> 00:00:51.370
When we say lazy materialization, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:51.370 --> 00:01:00.382
The term deferred work receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
00:01:00.382 --> 00:01:09.394
The next sequence uses Four-variable truth layout as a conceptual teaching example, not as measured benchmark evidence.

q0009
00:01:09.394 --> 00:01:13.382
Our stable example is Four-variable truth layout.

q0010
00:01:13.382 --> 00:01:22.802
F(A,B,C,D)=(A AND B) XOR (C OR D), row variables A,B, column variables C,D, MSB-first ordering.

q0011
00:01:22.802 --> 00:01:30.307
Carry assignments, live support, explicit CM, packed truth vectors, and exact output across episodes.

q0012
00:01:30.307 --> 00:01:37.812
We now construct the Four-variable truth layout and name every part before interpreting it.

q0013
00:01:37.812 --> 00:01:47.232
Run matched timelines: the eager path constructs aligned arrays during compilation while the lazy path retains deferred structure.

q0014
00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:55.239
Request the final output and show the lazy materialization occurring once before exact outputs meet.

q0015
00:01:55.239 --> 00:02:00.232
Now isolate eager construction timing inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0016
00:02:00.232 --> 00:02:09.244
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for eager construction timing changes.

q0017
00:02:09.244 --> 00:02:18.256
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to eager construction timing, not to a substituted workload.

q0018
00:02:18.256 --> 00:02:24.756
Eager fills aligned regions early; lazy carries outlined placeholders until output demand.

q0019
00:02:24.756 --> 00:02:29.749
Now isolate lazy deferred materialization inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0020
00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:38.761
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for lazy deferred materialization changes.

q0021
00:02:38.761 --> 00:02:47.773
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to lazy deferred materialization, not to a substituted workload.

q0022
00:02:47.773 --> 00:02:57.193
The eager and lazy CM paths differ in when aligned dense work is materialized, not in the Boolean function returned.

q0023
00:02:57.193 --> 00:03:03.190
Read that statement only within this scope: current eager/lazy implementations.

q0024
00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:07.178
Its declared measurement boundary is construction timing.

q0025
00:03:07.178 --> 00:03:11.166
The uncertainty field says no performance ranking.

q0026
00:03:11.166 --> 00:03:20.586
The nearest confusing lesson is Packed truth vectors: big integers, machine words, and masks; it owns packed truth-vector ordering, while this episode owns eager construction timing.

q0027
00:03:20.586 --> 00:03:30.006
The example fixes F of A, B, C, and D as A AND B, exclusive-or C OR D.

q0028
00:03:30.006 --> 00:03:36.003
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate eager construction timing.

q0029
00:03:36.003 --> 00:03:45.423
A and B select the row, C and D select the column, and MSB-first order fixes both index conventions.

q0030
00:03:45.423 --> 00:03:51.420
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate lazy deferred materialization.

q0031
00:03:51.420 --> 00:04:00.840
Every four-bit assignment names exactly one of the sixteen cells, and every cell returns one exact output bit.

q0032
00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:08.847
Folding the truth-table output column into a four-by-four grid changes the layout, not the function.

q0033
00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:18.267
Reading a cell forward evaluates an assignment; reading it backward recovers the row and column bits that selected it.

q0034
00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:27.687
Live support can remove an input from active computation even when the ambient layout still reserves its axis.

q0035
00:04:27.687 --> 00:04:37.107
A packed truth vector stores the same exact outputs in a different physical arrangement from the displayed matrix.

q0036
00:04:37.107 --> 00:04:46.527
The explicit matrix is dense by contract, so compactness and speed require separate evidence rather than definition alone.

q0037
00:04:46.527 --> 00:04:54.534
Holding variable order fixed makes matrix, packed-vector, and program views comparable without an indexing ambiguity.

q0038
00:04:54.534 --> 00:05:03.954
An exact equality check across the views is the gate before any timing ratio is allowed to matter.

q0039
00:05:03.954 --> 00:05:13.374
The starting state preserves the stable definition: F(A,B,C,D)=(A AND B) XOR (C OR D), row variables A,B, column variables C,D, MSB-first ordering.

q0040
00:05:13.374 --> 00:05:18.869
The implementation distinction does not establish a universal performance ranking.

q0041
00:05:18.869 --> 00:05:25.369
Place three construction and materialization steps on the eager or lazy timeline.

q0042
00:05:25.369 --> 00:05:29.357
Eager and lazy change scheduling, not semantics.

q0043
00:05:29.357 --> 00:05:36.359
A common mistake is this: Lazy means no materialization work is ever performed.

q0044
00:05:36.359 --> 00:05:42.356
Repair it by returning to the owned distinction: eager construction timing.

q0046
00:05:45.496 --> 00:05:53.001
Use the episode's central distinction to answer: Eager and lazy change scheduling, not semantics.

q0047
00:05:53.001 --> 00:06:00.003
Ask when the work occurs before asking how long the whole task takes.
